completed_at: "2026-10-02T19:46:24.853Z"
author: "harness:codex"
estimated_minutes: 240
acceptance_criteria: "Patch external Axios to a cooldown-eligible supported release and eliminate affected CJS/ESM bundled copies with reproducible integrity and source-map evidence.; Preserve CodSpeed instrumentation, platform compatibility, benchmark coverage and package contracts; retain genuine pre-fix vulnerability controls.; Enforce development dependency vulnerability admission in mandatory CI, nightly, release and local gates; seeded vulnerable artifacts must fail without changing coverage or quality thresholds.; Verify full and production audits, dev-inclusive Trivy, real Node/Bun tooling and merged-main Scorecard retirement; document evidence tiers without suppressing or dismissing an unresolved report."
parent: pm-qwoy
risk: high
confidence: high
resolution: "CodSpeed CJS/ESM entries use audited dedicated Axios clients with preserved cancellation and FormData contracts; obsolete embedded sources and maps are removed, native bytes remain intact, and exact twelve-file inventory plus hashes and development-inclusive audit/Trivy admission reject recurrence. Shared secret detection preserves real credential refusal while recognizing the public empty-fallback expression."
expected_result: "Installed tooling contains no affected external or embedded Axios, and mandatory admission preserves runtime, native tooling and SDK security contracts."
actual_result: "All-severity and production audits report zero; exact twelve-file hashes and inventory controls pass. Real CJS/ESM HTTP and interceptor controls, 47 focused tests, static/typecheck/secrets/docs gates and refreshed packed/dogfood consumers pass. Canonical PM receipt test-local-murdbyvj-6ohpqa passes 9608 tests; report receipt test-local-murdgisu-s8759q records statements 66411/66411, branches 50825/50825, functions 13734/13734 and lines 63334/63334. Revised-head native performance and merged-main Scorecard alert 29 retirement remain explicit independent checks under open pm-7zs0; no alert was dismissed and publication is not claimed."
